# The SQLite that rusqlite bundles, as a C library, for the difftests on
# Linux: a difftest links the C++ oracle, whose mbgl-core brings the C++
# core's vendored SQLite (3.45), and the port, whose rusqlite brings its
# bundled SQLite (3.54). rustc puts the oracle's libraries before the Rust
# crates, and lld resolves rusqlite's references from the earlier SQLite
# archive, then pulls the bundled one for the newer functions: duplicate
# symbols. Listed first in link_deps, this archive comes first on the link
# line, so lld resolves every SQLite reference of both sides from it and
# pulls neither of the other two. On macOS the
# oracle uses the system SQLite instead and the duplicate cannot happen.
alias(
    name = "sqlite",
    actual = "@libsqlite3_sys//:sqlite3",
    visibility = ["//difftest:__subpackages__"],
)
